<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Hutton Brew</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1844–1915</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Hutton Brew was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> lawyer and journalist of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> and British descent. He was one of the Western-educated leaders of the Fante Confederacy in the early 1870s and helped draft its constitution. He later founded some of the first African-owned newspapers in the Gold Coast, including the Gold Coast Times in 1874, and criticised British colonial rule before settling in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p></div>
